{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2194-01-17 15:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee, one of your surgical team doctors. We're admitting you today for that non-healing ulcer on your left foot. Do you have any questions so far?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2194-01-17 15:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. Yes, I’ve been worried. Last time I was here, I got pneumonia and couldn’t have the procedure. Is it safe to do it now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2194-01-17 15:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a great question. We reviewed your recent chest X-ray from earlier today. There’s clear improvement in the pneumonia. Your cough has mostly resolved, and you haven’t had fevers. So yes, we feel it’s safe to proceed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2194-01-17 15:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. What exactly will you be doing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2194-01-17 15:41:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll do an angiogram to look at the blood flow in your left leg. Then, we plan to place a stent in the popliteal artery behind your knee to improve circulation to your foot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2194-01-17 15:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the ulcer? Will that heal better after?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2194-01-17 15:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Better blood flow helps wounds heal. We’ll keep up with daily dressing changes, and you’ll continue the collagenase ointment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2194-01-17 15:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my transplant meds? I increased my tacrolimus to 2 mg twice a day after last discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2194-01-17 15:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve noted that. Transplant nephrology is involved, and we’ll check your tacrolimus levels every morning to keep it in the right range."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2194-01-17 15:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve also had some diarrhea off and on. Should I restart the loperamide?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2194-01-17 15:53:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor that. Since it’s not happening now, we won’t restart it yet. But if it returns, we can."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2194-01-17 15:55:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. And my heart? I know I have the mechanical valve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2194-01-17 15:57:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re managing your anticoagulation carefully. You’re on IV heparin now. Before the procedure, we’ll check your INR. If it’s too high, we may give fresh frozen plasma."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2194-01-17 15:59:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that from last time. And after the stent, I’ll need both aspirin and coumadin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2194-01-17 16:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. That helps keep the stent open. You’ll continue both long-term."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2194-01-17 16:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And when will the procedure happen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2194-01-17 16:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Tomorrow morning. Today, we’ll do some final checks, including another set of labs and your dialysis session."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2194-01-17 16:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had dialysis earlier today. Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2194-01-17 16:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect timing. That helps us optimize your labs before surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2194-01-17 16:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my foot still feels very sensitive, even though I don’t have pain. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2194-01-17 16:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, with your history of diabetes and neuropathy, that’s common. We’ll keep protecting the area and checking pulses daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2194-01-18 07:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs look stable. The PTT is therapeutic at 70.7, so we’ll continue the heparin at 800 units per hour."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2194-01-18 07:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my INR? I know it was high last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2194-01-18 07:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR was elevated, so we gave two units of fresh frozen plasma this morning. That should help bring it down before the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2194-01-18 07:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’m ready when you are."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2194-01-18 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, we’re back from the procedure. Everything went well. We placed a Zilver stent in your left popliteal artery and used a spider filter during the procedure to catch any debris."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2194-01-18 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. Did the blood flow improve?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2194-01-18 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the angiogram showed good flow after stenting. Your left foot has dopplerable pulses and is warm, which is a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2194-01-18 13:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the groin site? Any issues?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2194-01-18 13:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We closed the access site with a Perclose device. No bleeding, and we’ll keep an eye on it for hematoma."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2194-01-18 13:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel a bit tired. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2194-01-18 13:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Absolutely. You’ll rest here for a few hours. We’ll keep you on IV fluids and restart your coumadin tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2194-01-18 13:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the heparin will continue?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2194-01-18 13:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll restart the IV heparin at 800 units per hour tonight and continue it until your INR is therapeutic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2194-01-19 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re doing well. Your PTT is now 74.2, which is in the therapeutic range. We’ll discharge you today to extended care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2194-01-19 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "To rehab? Will they manage my heparin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2194-01-19 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, they’ll continue the IV heparin until your INR reaches the goal. You’ll keep taking aspirin and coumadin daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2194-01-19 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my foot? Should I keep it elevated?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2194-01-19 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, elevate it above heart level when sitting. Avoid standing too long. And no heavy lifting for a week to protect the groin site."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2194-01-19 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "When should I call the office?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2194-01-19 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you have new pain, coldness, or numbness in your leg, a fever over 101.5, or any bleeding from the groin. And keep up with your wound care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2194-01-19 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2194-01-19 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. You did great. We’ll see you in follow-up in four weeks."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2194-01-17 15:33:00",
    "admission_end": "2194-01-19 18:38:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a complex medical history including end-stage renal disease, a transplanted pancreas and kidney, mechanical mitral valve, and peripheral vascular disease was admitted for revascularization of a non-healing left lower extremity ulcer. She had previously developed pneumonia during a prior admission, delaying the procedure. This time, her pulmonary status had improved, and a chest X-ray showed resolution of the prior infiltrate. She underwent successful left popliteal artery stenting with restoration of blood flow. The procedure was uncomplicated, and her left foot remained warm with dopplerable pulses. Anticoagulation was managed with IV heparin and bridging to coumadin, with fresh frozen plasma given preoperatively due to elevated INR. She remained afebrile, with stable vital signs and no signs of infection. She was discharged to extended care on IV heparin, aspirin, and coumadin, with plans for vascular surgery follow-up in four weeks.",
    "problems": [
      "Ulcer of other part of lower limb",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Systolic heart failure, unspecified",
      "Pancreas replaced by transplant",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease, unspecified, with chronic kidney disease stage V or end stage renal disease",
      "Chronic glomerulonephritis with lesion of membranous glomerulonephritis",
      "Kidney replaced by transplant",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Peripheral vascular disease, unspecified",
      "Mitral valve disorders",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of unspecified type of vessel, native or graft",
      "Aortocoronary bypass status",
      "Acquired absence of both cervix and uterus",
      "Heart valve replaced by other means",
      "Renal dialysis status",
      "Old myocardial infarction",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Automatic implantable cardiac defibrillator in situ"
    ]
  }
}
